/-!
# Independent batches of recovered-word matrix equations

The numerical certificate is split into four consecutive batches. Each batch
refers to the same explicitly supplied family of matrices, so its equations
can be checked independently of the other batches. Combining the batches
constructs the original `RecoveredWordProgram.Certificate` without adding
any mathematical premise to that certificate.

The equations are precisely those of `WordValues/Certificate.lean`, from
Breuer–Magaard–Wilson (2019), Table 1 and §3.4; provenance and the source DAG
are documented in `../../source/README.md`. The owner of the numerical
certificate must supply all four batches and identify both output matrices.
-/

public section
